### Quick fix you can drop in

```go
var (
    cacheMu sync.RWMutex
    cache   = map[string]string{}
)

func Get(key string) (string, error) {
    // fast read‑only path
    cacheMu.RLock()
    if v, ok := cache[key]; ok {
        cacheMu.RUnlock()
        return v, nil
    }
    cacheMu.RUnlock()

    // miss – load (outside lock!)
    v, err := load(key)
    if err != nil {
        return "", err
    }

    // store the result
    cacheMu.Lock()
    cache[key] = v
    cacheMu.Unlock()
    return v, nil
}
```

Replace `load` with a version that returns `(string, error)` so you can propagate failures.

---

**Bottom line:** The original code is unsafe for any real concurrent workload. Guard the map, make the write visible before returning, and (optionally) add eviction or use a battle‑tested caching library. That will give you a reliable, race‑free cache.
